l":771449,"votes":{"kennedy":362327,"nixon":404521,"other":4601},"evs":{"nixon":12}},"WA":{"ev":9,"method":"popular","total":1241572,"votes":{"kennedy":599298,"nixon":629273,"other":13001},"evs":{"nixon":9}},"WV":{"ev":8,"method":"popular","total":837781,"votes":{"kennedy":441786,"nixon":395995},"evs":{"kennedy":8}},"WI":{"ev":12,"method":"popular","total":1729082,"votes":{"kennedy":830805,"nixon":895175,"other":3102},"evs":{"nixon":12}},"WY":{"ev":3,"method":"popular","total":140782,"votes":{"kennedy":63331,"nixon":77451},"evs":{"nixon":3}}},"notes":["This was the first election in which Alaska and Hawaii took part, so 50 states cast electoral votes.","In Alabama, voters chose each of the 11 electors individually. Of the Democratic electors, 5 were pledged to Kennedy and 6 were unpledged.","Harry F. Byrd was not on the ballot but received 15 electoral votes: 6 from the unpledged Democratic electors chosen in Alabama, 8 from those chosen in Mississippi, and 1 from Henry D. Irwin, an Oklahoma elector pledged to Nixon. For vice president, the unpledged electors voted for Strom Thurmond, and Irwin voted for Barry Goldwater.","In Alabama, Kennedy is credited with the vote for his highest-polling elector (318,303) and the unpledged electors with 324,050, out of 570,225 ballots. Most Democratic voters chose electors from both slates, so Alabama’s shares add up to more than 100%.","For the same reason the national shares, counting Alabama’s votes for both slates, add up to a little more than 100%. Kennedy’s and Nixon’s shares are close to the usual figures, 49.72% and 49.55%.","Added up state by state, the unpledged electors have 610,409 votes. Wikipedia’s national table gives them 286,359, leaving out Alabama."],"corrections":{"AL":{"sources":["American Presidency Project, 1960 state-by-state table","Polidata, Alabama election history (state totals)","Wikipedia, 1960 United States presidential election in Alabama (general election table and county table, also read as raw 